    "updated_at": "2020-11-13T11:40:42Z",
    "body": "If you don't need stuff like the command duration module you should be able to use most starship features in any shell if you set your prompt to execute `starship prompt`. You should be able to use something like that until somebody implements official tcsh support.\r\n\r\nI also recommend setting `STARSHIP_SHELL` to `tcsh` or maybe `bash` or `zsh` if that fixes display issues.\r\n\r\nI think it might be harder to support the [command duration module](https://starship.rs/config/#command-duration), but stuff like `--status` (last exit code) and `--jobs` (number of running jobs) should be easy to implement. (For more info about those arguments look at the othe init scripts in` src/init` and `starship prompt --help`.",
